From b562a768419c887d6d595deeef2d1bac1f18ff44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mariolopez <mariolopez@jisap.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:47:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Harden patching: validate write targets, check results,
 avoid OOB reads

- Route all code patches through writeCode(): reject targets outside an
  executable section of termsrv.dll and report WriteProcessMemory failures.
- Route data flags through writeFlag(): only write inside writable sections
  instead of blindly dereferencing a decoded displacement.
- Guard the "CUtils::" lookback when IsSingleSessionPerUser is not found
  (previously read before the image base).
- pattenMatch: never read past the mapped section or the pattern end.
- findSection: compare 8-byte section names correctly.
- findImportFunction: skip imports by ordinal.
- PropertyDeviceAddr: only follow jumps with a relative immediate operand.
- Initialise bRemoteConnAllowed_xref.
- DllMain: fail the load if ServiceMain is missing, null-check
  SvchostPushServiceGlobals, check Thread32First.
- Log every applied patch (name + RVA) via OutputDebugString.
- TermWrapTest: print a byte diff of the image before/after patch().

Verified: identical patch output to v0.7 on termsrv.dll 10.0.26100.1,
.9444, .9549 and .9818; unrelated DLLs no longer crash the test harness.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
